Blinkit Sales Analysis Dashboard – Power BI

📌 Project Overview

This project presents an interactive Blinkit Sales Analysis Dashboard developed using Microsoft Power BI. The main purpose of the project is to understand sales performance across different outlet types, outlet sizes, locations, and product categories.
The dashboard converts raw sales data into meaningful visual insights so that business performance can be understood quickly and easily. It focuses on identifying important sales patterns and comparing different outlet characteristics.

🎯 Project Objectives

The major objectives of this project are:
Analyze overall sales performance.
Understand how outlet type affects sales.
Analyze the relationship between outlet size and total sales.
Study sales distribution across different outlet locations.
Compare important business metrics across outlet types.
Identify product categories contributing to overall sales.
Present the findings through an interactive and easy-to-understand Power BI dashboard.

🛠️ Tools & Technologies Used

Microsoft Power BI – Data visualization and dashboard development
Power Query – Data cleaning and transformation
DAX – Creating calculated measures and KPIs
Excel/CSV Dataset – Source data
GitHub – Project documentation and version control

📊 Dashboard Analysis

The dashboard contains multiple visualizations designed to answer important business questions.

1. Sales by Item Type
Objective:
Analyze total sales across different item/product types and identify the categories contributing the most to overall revenue.
Chart Type: Bar/Column Chart

2. Sales by Outlet Type
Objective:
Compare sales performance between different outlet types and understand which outlet type generates higher sales.
Chart Type: Bar/Column Chart

3. Sales by Fat Content
Objective:
Analyze sales based on the fat-content classification of products and understand customer purchasing patterns.
Chart Type: Donut/Pie Chart

4. Sales by Outlet Establishment Year
Objective:
Analyze how sales have changed according to the year in which outlets were established.
Chart Type: Line Chart

5. Sales by Outlet Size
Objective:
Analyze the correlation between outlet size and total sales and identify which outlet size contributes the most to revenue.
Chart Type: Donut/Pie Chart

6. Sales by Outlet Location
Objective:
Assess the geographic distribution of sales across different outlet locations and understand the contribution of each location.
Chart Type: Funnel/Map Visualization

7. All Metrics by Outlet Type
Objective:
Provide a detailed comparison of important business metrics across different outlet types.
Chart Type: Matrix/Table or Comparison Visualization

📌 Key KPIs

The dashboard provides important performance indicators such as:
Total Sales
Average Sales
Number of Items
Average Rating
Outlet Count

These KPIs provide a quick overview of the overall business performance.

💡 Business Insights
The dashboard helps identify several useful patterns:
Sales performance varies across different outlet types.
Outlet size has an important relationship with overall sales.
Different locations contribute differently to total revenue.
Product/item categories show different levels of customer demand.
Outlet establishment year can be used to understand sales trends over time.
Comparing multiple metrics by outlet type helps identify stronger-performing outlet segments.

The dashboard can therefore support better decision-making related to outlet performance, product demand, and sales strategy.

📈 Dashboard Features
The Power BI dashboard is designed to be interactive and user-friendly.

Users can:
